Good reply. I never sat down to actually work out the time required to write
every bit 5 million times, but I had had some SCSI Flash drives myself at
one time. I bougth 5 for $10.00 each, 20MB each and SCSI too.

I figured I got them so cheap because they must have been reaching their
lifetime and there was a counter inside keeping track of writes.SO, I resold
them to someone who was a collector of computer things, he worked a QNX. I
suspect a real time system can make efficient use of this kind of disk
storage. I suspect a Multi-Tasking system such as OpenVMS would eat any
remaining life out of cheaply acquired unique hardware like this fairly
quickly.

Anyhow, that was my reasoning on the matter, just an alternative. I like the
idea of writelocking and booting OpenVMS, you'd definitely boot standalone
backup fairly fast this way.

Regards and have fun with the flash disks.

