You were right not to force it. The bezel is held on by screws from
behind. If you remove the PDP from the rack you can get at these
screws which will enable you to remove the bezel. You can then remove
the PDP from the rack which will enable you ... :-)

Seriously, though, whilst not on a slide, it is (at least the ones I
have are) in a wrap-around shell case which is what you see screwed to
the rack. It should pull out from the front, but the case is tight and
some effort is required. Purchase a new set of fingernails before
starting, or use a screwdriver as lever between the bezel and case if
the rack sides permit. The shell case is open at the bottom, so if you
can slide out what is below the PDP, you can get a hand in. There
shouldn't be any cables behind the bezel, but ...

