"okc.engineer" <okc.engineer@swbell.net> wrote in message news:<YxWLc.19097$cg1.14934@newssvr24.news.prodigy.com>...
> The VT100 terminal is DOA, so I can't use it.  I do have access to a 
> Televideo 905, but I don't know what the baud rate and communication 
> protocols are.

That depends on how your serial card is strapped, but a good place to
start is 9600 bps, 8N1.  In terms of protocols, most DEC serial ports
do not have hardware handshaking, but use XON/XOFF (^Q/^S) software
handshaking for flow control.

If locating a terminal is a problem, you can also use a variety of
personal computers (PCs, Macs, Amigas, Ataris, etc) with Kermit or
some other package that provides terminal emulation.


