>I turned off my Alphastation 200 this morning to add more
>memory.   Unfortunately, the power supply does not want to
>turn back on.   Does anyone have a spare?

Unfortunately, you'll find this is a common problem and spares are hard
to find (as is repair info, I figure this is probably a capacitor or
transistor blowing or something)

I recently replaced a Alphastation 200 power supply with a cheapo PC ATX 
supply.  I cut off the ATX supply connectors and soldered on the connectors
removed from the defunct Alphastation power supply.  Tedious but it now 
works fine. Note: Digital and the PC makers have different ideas what the 
color codes should be, don't blindly match wires of the same color.
Blue and yellow are swapped, for one.
