I would suggest to change the ribbon first; if the print head would be
bad, it would show a printout  with the whole area light, or, more
likely, a single pin would fail over the whole line. If it�s not the
ribbon, try to get some ( *very few* ) machine oil directly on the pins
before changing the head. Of course, you have to take the print head off
the machine to do so. Let the oil wet the pins in their guide, then wipe
off excessive oil before mounting the head into the printer again. This
helped with one of my own printers, and it�s serving me quite well,
again.

Frank


