I take it your controller doesn't have FRD and you don't have the Emulex 
MSCP formatter program FVD32M.

Okay, you can still do it the hard way.  Just take your time and be 
patient.  The early Emulex QD (And UD) MSCP controllers all used the 
same commands to initialize and program the NVRAM.  The early models 
didn't have FRD so a software diagnostic was necessary, or it could be 
toggled in.

Go here:

http://bitsavers.org/pdf/emulex/

Download the QD32 manual, see section 6.5.  It's exactly the same as the 
QD21.

FYI, early models of the Emulex contollers stored the bit for bad blocks 
differently than the later models.  If you changed out an old controller 
for a new one without reformatting the drive, it would report thousands 
of bad blocks even though the drive could be read correctly.  Corrective 
action was just to backup the drive, reformat and restore.

Good luck.



