> Another thing to try, which we used to do in the field when no spare
> head was available,on the LA-36, La-120 and La-180 heads is to clean
> the ribbon debris from the jewel where the pins are aligned in at the
> tip end of the print head. Take the print head off turn it upside down
> and place it in a small plastic cup with about a 1/2" of alcohol in
> the bottom, just enuff' to cover the tip of the print head pins as
> they pass thru the jewel. Let it soak for bout' 1/2 hour.
>
> Then shake off the excess alcohol from the head, let dry, remove any
> excess and dab a little oil at the tip off the head. Reinstall and try
> to print.
>
> This worked most of the time to free stuck pins and clean out the
> excess debris. Occasionally with a printer having a keyboard, after
> soaking the head we wud hold it tip side down, print characters on the
> keyboard to fire the pins and
> see the debris come free from the jewel.
>
> Good luck, fix the head no need to buy a new one if it is a stuck or
> bad pin.
>
